svg=['<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 800 560" role="img" aria-label="Hall footprint and ten conflicting course centers"><rect width="800" height="560" fill="#e7e6df"/><text x="30" y="25" font-family="sans-serif" font-size="16">Hall floor cut • north ↑ • schematic at model coordinates</text>',f'<path d="{path(s["replacementOuter"])}" fill="#83988a" stroke="#23483b"/>']
for ring in s['basementHoles']:svg.append(f'<path d="{path(ring)}" fill="#203d51" stroke="#fff"/>')
for i,p in enumerate(c['centerConflicts'],1):
 x,y=xy(p['center']['x'],-p['center']['z']);svg.append(f'<circle cx="{x}" cy="{y}" r="6" fill="#bd3b2e" stroke="white"/><text x="{x+8}" y="{y-6}" font-family="sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#782019">{i}</text>')
svg.append('<text x="30" y="535" font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14">Green: hall replacement • blue: basement wells • red: course-center conflicts</text></svg>');(out/'plan.svg').write_text(''.join(svg))
rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{i}</td><td>{html.escape(names[p["course"]])}</td><td>{p["feature"]}</td><td>{html.escape(p["observed"].get("surface") or p["message"])}</td></tr>'for i,p in enumerate(c['centerConflicts'],1))
(out/'index.html').write_text('''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Hall and concourse floor integration</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:24px;background:#f3f2ec;color:#18382f;font:16px/1.55 system-ui}a{color:#165b49}img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin:20px 0}h1{line-height:1.1}.notice{padding:16px;background:#f8e2c3}.table{overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #bacabd;text-align:left}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}</style><a href="../../index.html">Research library</a><h1>Connect the new hall to the existing concourse</h1><p class="notice">Uninstalled integration candidate. Floor partition and eight native walks pass. Ten authored course centers conflict with the reconstructed wells or escalators; course integration remains incomplete.</p><p>The cut removes 598.85 m² of the old concourse under the replacement footprint, retaining 14,047.15 m² and the existing western opening. Three basement wells total 145.88 m². Plain outer-floor material is an inspection stand-in.</p><a href="../HALL-CONCOURSE-JOIN.md">Evidence and limits</a><h2>Chrome geometry inspection</h2><img src="overview.png" alt="Isolated hall and retained concourse showing open basement wells"><img src="north.png" alt="Walking-height view of the joined floors and well guards"><h2>Course dependencies</h2><img src="plan.svg" alt="Model plan with ten conflicting centers"><p>74 authored centers from 17 courses were queried with a 0.1 m placement radius. This is a support audit, not a full disk-footprint or ball-trajectory test. Ten additional supported centers change surface identity.</p><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Map</th><th>Course</th><th>Feature</th><th>Observed support or rejection</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+rows+'''</tbody></table></div><h2>Receipts</h2><ul><li><a href="interface-proof.json">Exact floor partition and unchanged assembly</a></li><li><a href="serialization.json">Browser/native serialization</a></li><li><a href="course-summary.json">All conflicts and surface identity changes</a></li><li><a href="source-depth.json">Municipal mesh depth audit</a></li></ul></html>''')
